{"id": "EUVD-2026-103519", "enisaUuid": "ae743255-a369-3578-9426-a215da2fd25d", "description": "libdvdnav before 7.0.0 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in dvdnav_describe_title_chapters that allows attackers to read beyond the part-of-title array by supplying an oversized vts_ttn value. Attackers can provide a crafted DVD or disc image declaring a larger VMGI title vts_ttn than the title set's entries to crash applications enumerating chapters.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T12:19:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T17:58:02", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/libdvdnav-navigation-index-oob-read", "https://code.videolan.org/videolan/libdvdnav/-/blob/6.1.1/src/searching.c#L670", "https://code.videolan.org/videolan/libdvdnav/-/commit/1d2af48d685911a169fe77d500b1d426910c6f77", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libdvdnav-before-7.0.0-out-of-bounds-read-in-dvdnav-describe-title-chapters"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112057", "GHSA-2m5j-rc78-vx58"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "83f32506-de89-328f-b559-1d3822ff86b4", "product": {"name": "libdvdnav", "vendor": {"name": "VideoLAN"}}, "product_version": "0 <7.0.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "dd2edaae-7af8-30bd-94ce-6a88e518006d", "vendor": {"name": "VideoLAN"}}], "isExploited": false}